# Blurz Football — Legacy Football Game Engine Modernization

## 1. Project Context

This project is an Android native football game based on a legacy football-game codebase whose original design dates back roughly 15+ years.

The current project already contains a substantial native C++ engine, Android integration, OpenGL ES rendering infrastructure, game entities, assets, scenes, input/HID abstractions, schedulers, managers, UI systems, physics, audio, and football-specific gameplay code.

The objective is **not** to throw away the existing project and create a completely new game from scratch.

The objective is to **modernize, stabilize, reorganize, and progressively evolve the existing game into a maintainable modern mobile football game**, while preserving useful existing technology and assets whenever practical.

The modernization should ultimately provide:

* A reliable modern game loop
* Functional player movement
* Functional virtual controls
* Modern input architecture
* Modern rendering architecture
* Modern football gameplay architecture
* Modern UI
* Better player models
* Player characteristics and visual identity
* Modern stadium/pitch presentation
* Modern match HUD
* Scalable team/player data
* Clean separation between Android/Java UI and native C++ gameplay
* Maintainable source code
* Testable systems
* Extensible architecture
* Production-oriented project organization

The goal is **not complexity for its own sake**.

Prefer simple, understandable engineering over excessive abstractions or unnecessary frameworks.

