# 3. Critical Rule: Inspect Before Modifying

Before changing architecture or writing substantial code:

1. Inspect the complete repository.
2. Identify the current entry points.
3. Identify how Android starts the native engine.
4. Identify how Java communicates with C++.
5. Identify the current game loop.
6. Identify the current rendering pipeline.
7. Identify how scenes are created.
8. Identify how players are represented.
9. Identify how teams are represented.
10. Identify how the ball is represented.
11. Identify how input is currently handled.
12. Identify why player movement currently does not work.
13. Identify why virtual joysticks/buttons do not work.
14. Identify the current UI architecture.
15. Identify existing physics functionality.
16. Identify existing animation functionality.
17. Identify existing database/data structures.
18. Identify which systems are functional, partially functional, obsolete, or dead code.

Do not assume that the existing architecture is correct simply because the code already exists.

Do not rewrite functioning systems without understanding their purpose.

Produce an initial **legacy-system audit** before major refactoring.

