# 6. Do Not Force One Architecture Everywhere

The project contains fundamentally different types of code.

Do not force gameplay entities, rendering objects, Android UI, database access, and low-level OpenGL code into the same abstraction model.

Use appropriate architecture for each subsystem.

For example:

```text
Gameplay
→ component/system-oriented where useful

Rendering
→ render pipeline / scene-oriented

Android UI
→ platform UI architecture

Data
→ repositories/data models

Input
→ action-based abstraction

Platform
→ adapters
```

The architecture should remain understandable to a developer who did not create the original engine.

