# 12. Player Movement

The first gameplay milestone should be extremely simple:

> Put one player on the pitch and make the player move correctly using the virtual joystick.

Before implementing complete football gameplay, prove that this pipeline works:

```text
Touch
 ↓
Joystick
 ↓
Input
 ↓
PlayerController
 ↓
Movement
 ↓
Animation
 ↓
Rendering
```

Acceptance criteria:

* Joystick moves visually.
* Joystick direction reaches C++.
* Player moves in the intended direction.
* Player speed is frame-rate independent.
* Player rotates toward movement direction.
* Player stops correctly when joystick is released.
* Player animation changes appropriately.

Only after this works should the full team controller be implemented.

