# 50. AI Coding Agent Behavior

When working on this repository:

### Before coding

Explain:

* What you discovered
* What currently works
* What is broken
* What the relevant code path is
* Why the existing implementation fails
* What the smallest correct fix is

### Before major refactoring

Explain:

* Current architecture
* Target architecture
* Migration path
* Files that will change
* Risks
* How the change will be tested

### During implementation

Make small, logically isolated changes.

Do not modify unrelated systems.

### After implementation

Provide:

* Files changed
* What changed
* Why it changed
* Build/test result
* Remaining limitations
* Next recommended step

Never claim a feature is functional without verifying the actual execution path.

